tatus per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.thm-signed-periodic"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.thm-signed-periodic"],"id":"long.thm-signed-periodic","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.23 (A formal dichotomy for signed periodic weights)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.23, p. 50, label thm:signed-periodic","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Let $b\\ge2$ and $m\\ge1$ be integers, and let $w:\\mathbb{N}_{>0}\\to\\mathbb{Z}$ be $m$-periodic. Put\n$$\nx=\\sum_{a\\ge1}\\frac{w(a)}{b^a-1},\\qquad\n c_w(n)=\\sum_{d\\mid n}w(d).\n$$\nThe cited formal argument gives the dichotomy that $x$ is irrational or $b^kx\\in\\mathbb{Z}$ for some integer $k\\ge0$. It excludes the latter alternative if $c_w$ has one sign throughout and is nonzero at arbitrarily large indices. These sign assumptions concern $c_w$, not $w$. As noted above, Luca and Tachiya’s theorem already excludes the terminating alternative for every nonzero periodic $w$, without either sign restriction. The zero weight gives $x=0$.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.thm-signed-periodic","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.thm-signed-periodic","id":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.thm-signed-periodic%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.irrational_intWeightedErdosSeries_periodic_of_coeff_nonneg_of_frequently_ne_zero%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.thm-signed-periodic%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.irrational_intWeightedErdosSeries_periodic_of_coeff_nonneg_of_frequently_ne_zero%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c